# the devthink docker build context.
# The docker build context carries the sources only: THE Dockerfile builds
# from a clean checkout — the deps stage installs the frozen bun.lock tree
# itself, the builder compiles every dist target and runs the deterministic
# checks, and the runtime copies only the lean output. The local
# node_modules trees, the built dist, the committed distpackage staging
# (the builder stages its own), the release scratch, the mobile capacitor
# shell (a native wrapper concern, never a container input), the packaged
# archives and the development state never enter the image.
.git
# the workflow corpus stays in the build context: the gate ladder the
# container image runs (npm test) reads .github/workflows through the
# workflowcheck, readiness and publishing-pipeline contracts, so the
# workflows travel with the sources into the builder stage only — the
# runtime stages copy their lean outputs and never ship the corpus.
.github/*
!.github/workflows
.manus-logs
node_modules
sol/node_modules
mobile
dist
distpackage
build
sol/dist
release
staging
*.tgz
*.zip
*.xpi
*.vsix
*.tar.gz
*.log
*.sqlite
*.db
.env
.env.*
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
test/tmp

# the monorepo geometry (the 2.0.186 cure): the merged repository carries
# eleven sibling app trees whose node_modules, dist and staging the runner
# installs beside the sources — the family-context law keeps the sibling
# SOURCES (the vault file: pins, the getry and saddle bridges) while their
# dependency trees never enter the transfer (the 22.8GB context the smoke
# lane measured never rides again; the deps stage installs the frozen
# locks itself).
*/node_modules
*/dist
*/distpackage
*/build
*/release
*/staging
*/sol/dist
*/sol/node_modules
*/test/tmp
*/mobile
**/__pycache__
tool-results
